Make `init_active_samples()` a no-op so concurrent `eval_async` calls
don't clear each other's `ActiveSample` entries.

With the reentrancy guard lifted (`inspect-eval-async-guard.patch`), a
second `eval_async` would `.clear()` the first's entries; the first's
per-sample teardown then hits `list.remove(x): x not in list` and the
eval finishes `status='error'`. The list is process-global by design
(the ctl server reads it across evals); per-sample append/remove keeps
it bounded.

Apply on `inspect_ai` `model-event-output-streaming` (upstream candidate).
Depends on: `inspect-eval-async-guard.patch`.
Rationale: `collaborative-auditor` `src/workbench/m1/M1-RUN-AUDITS.md` §guard.

